    "result_text": "BUILD SUCCESS \u2014 the only test class in the project (`AcceptanceTest`) passes, along with a clean full build.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented `customerCode` assignment formatted `<LAST3>-<NNNN>` on owner creation.\n\nChanges, kept as small cohesive additions rather than growing any method:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `customerCode` property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes it and MapStruct auto-maps it (no mapper change needed).\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a persisted `customerCode` field with a plain getter/setter (one-liners, no surrounding complexity added).\n\n3. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 two lines before save: derive `LAST3` from the upper-cased first three letters of `lastName`, and set the code to `String.format(\"%s-%04d\", last3, ownerCount + 1)` where the count is taken *before* persisting, giving \"one more than the current number of owners\" (a global sequence, since `findAllOwners()` flushes and counts the previously-created owner within the same transaction).\n\n4. **`db/hsqldb/schema.sql`** / **`data.sql`** \u2014 added the `customer_code` column (test profile uses `ddl-auto=none`) and padded the 10 positional seed inserts with `NULL`.\n\nThe hook lives in the small controller method and the derivation is a single expression, so no method's cyclomatic complexity grew and no large class absorbed new logic. The behavior matches the spec (e.g. 7th owner named \"Smithers\" \u2192 `SMI-0007`) and the test asserting `cb == ca + 1` with `SMI-`/`JON-` prefixes passes.",
